<p>This is surprising: When water is poured from one container into another, floating particles can climb upstream, like inanimate salmon, into the higher container. Argentine physicist Sebastian Bianchini first noticed the phenomenon while making tea during his studies at the University of Havana. <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1105.2585">His paper</a> inspired further work at Rutgers, which has confirmed the effect, but exactly what&#8217;s happening isn&#8217;t fully understood.</p>
